     "text": "… reached Pakistan with only the clothes on their bodies. Countless among them had come after sacrificing their dear ones and relatives. They needed not only shelter and employment but were also in dire need of being brought out of psychological pressure. The rehabilitation of these refugees was a very great challenge for a country like Pakistan. However, the inhabitants of Pakistan faced this challenge with great courage and spirit. To look after the refugees the Quaid-e-Azam himself went to Lahore, raised the morale of the refugees and supervised their rehabilitation.",
