   "theory": "Questions\n\n1. Fill in the blanks with suitable words.\n\ni. The last Viceroy of India was ________ .\n\nii. The first Prime Minister of Bharat was ________ .\n\niii. In the Punjab Boundary Commission Pakistan was represented by Justice Din Muhammad and ________ .\n\niv. Pakistan’s share in the joint cash assets of India was fixed at ________ million rupees.\n\nv. The decision to partition India was made under the ________ plan.\n\nvi. The Indus Basin Treaty was signed on ________ .\n\nvii. The first Constituent Assembly of Pakistan was presided over by ________ .\n\n2. Choose the correct word from the words given in brackets.\n\ni. The first Governor-General of Pakistan was ________ . (Liaquat Ali Khan, Khawaja Nazimuddin, the Quaid-e-Azam, Ghulam Muhammad)\n\nii. The first Prime Minister of Pakistan was ________ . (Sardar Abdur Rab Nishtar, Liaquat Ali Khan, Abdul Qayyum Khan, Maulvi Fazal-ul-Haq)\n\niii. The population of tehsil Batala (district Gurdaspur) consisted of ________ per cent Muslims. (50, 65, 70, 77)\n\niv. Field Marshal Auchinleck was removed from his post on the complaint of ________ . (Gandhi, the Quaid-e-Azam, Pandit Nehru, Lord Mountbatten)\n\nv. In the canal water dispute between Pakistan and Bharat, the area of Pakistan’s province of ________ was most affected. (Sarhad, Punjab, Sindh, Azad Kashmir)",
