   "content": "<p>3. Identify the correct and incorrect among the following.</p><p>i. Sir Cyril Radcliffe presented the plan for the partition of India.</p><p>ii. With the inclusion of Pathankot in Bharat it got the land route to reach Kashmir.</p><p>iii. Calcutta was the capital of the province of Bengal.</p><p>iv. After the establishment of Pakistan the country did not face any shortage of government employees.</p><p>v. Gandhi helped get Pakistan its share in the joint assets.</p><p>4. Write short answers to the following.</p><p>i. Which areas acquired disputed status under the Radcliffe Award?</p><p>ii. Why was Pakistan entangled in problems at the time of partition?</p><p>iii. Why was the Muslim-majority area of district Gurdaspur included in Bharat?</p><p>iv. Why was Field Marshal Auchinleck removed from his post?</p><p>v. What did the Quaid-e-Azam urge students most?</p><p>5. Keeping the historical background in view, present a possible solution to the Kashmir problem.</p><p>6. Why did the canal water dispute arise between Pakistan and Bharat? What steps did both countries take to solve it? Write a comprehensive note.</p><p>7. Throw light on the leadership abilities of the Quaid-e-Azam as Governor-General of Pakistan.</p><p>8. Which qualities are necessary for a good leader?</p><p>9. In your opinion, what can be the best solution of disputes between nations? Discuss in the present global context.</p>",
