   "content": "<p>Map: Regions of Pakistan by climate</p><p>3) The region of the lower Indus valley and the Thar desert</p><p>In the southern and eastern Indus valley a desert condition is found. Here in summer there is intense heat by day. Hot, dry “loo” and dusty dust-storms blow, because of which work becomes difficult. At night, however, the temperature falls. The people here wear loose clothes and tie turbans on their heads so that they may remain protected from the heat of the sun, the loo and the hot sandy wind. The winter season is short. The common occupation of the people here is herding. In areas where irrigation is arranged, cultivation is done. People live in open and airy houses. The walls of the houses are thick and made of mud. In areas where the sea breeze reaches, wind-catchers facing the sea have been built on the roofs of the houses. The aim of all these things is to keep the houses airy and cool in summer. In areas where there is a lot of sand, transport is difficult; people travel by night on camels. Sometimes this area also falls victim to drought. Because of shortage of water and fodder, livestock suffer great loss of life.</p><p>4) The Balochistan Plateau region of continental climate</p><p>The climate of the Balochistan Plateau is also of the extreme type. Lack of rain and water has badly affected the whole of Balochistan. This area is mostly arid, i.e. dry and desert-like. In summer there is great heat. Sibi and Loralai, among the hottest areas, also lie in this region. At the foot of the mountains, where a little water is available, irrigation is done there by means of underground channels or karez to avoid evaporation. In the eastern and north-eastern part of the region, thanks to the cold and dry climate, fruits are produced in abundance. According to one estimate Balochistan provides 45 per cent of Pakistan’s fruits.</p><p>5) The coastal region of maritime climate</p><p>Going southwards one comes to the coastal area, where because of the nearness of the sea the climate is moderate and humid. Because of the humid climate there are more cotton-cloth factories in Karachi, since the thread does not break because of the humidity. For the cultivation of palm trees the climate of the coastal area …</p>",
