   "theory": "Exercise\n\n1. Fill in the blanks with suitable words.\n\ni. The Wakhan strip, an area of Afghanistan, separates Pakistan from ________ .\n\nii. The Islamic world is spread from Morocco in the west to ________ in the east.\n\niii. Trade with China takes place by way of ________ .\n\niv. The sandy area between the rivers Indus and Jhelum is called ________ .\n\nv. After the Second World War ________ was given the status of a regular industry.\n\nvi. Scales are generally expressed in ________ ways.\n\n2. Identify the correct and incorrect among the following.\n\ni. The Arabian Sea lies to the south of Pakistan.\n\nii. Pakistan lies at the last edge of the Islamic world.\n\niii. Sibi and Jacobabad are counted among the hottest places in the world.\n\niv. K-2 is the highest peak in the world.\n\nv. The Karakoram Highway is called the seventh wonder of the world.\n\n3. Choose the correct word from the words given in brackets.\n\ni. Nankana Sahib is the holy place of the followers of which religion? (Hindu, Sikh, Buddhist, Jain)\n\nii. Which province provides 45% of Pakistan’s fruits? (Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Punjab, Sindh, Balochistan)\n\niii. How much time does each longitude take to pass in front of the sun? (2 minutes, 4 minutes, 6 minutes, 10 minutes)",
