     "text": "The provincial assembly is elected for five years. The Governor can dissolve the assembly on the advice of the provincial Chief Minister. But in such a case the Governor will have to hold elections within a hundred days to form a new assembly. The Governor can himself also send recommendations relating to legislation to the provincial assembly, and it will be bound to give them consideration.",
