     "text": "He gave public welfare priority over other works. For the first time in the history of the world he fixed stipends for needy people. Salaries were paid to the disabled and the destitute from the Bait-ul-Mal. He had guest houses built in most cities, where travellers were fed at the expense of the Bait-ul-Mal. In Madina a public langar (free kitchen) was set up for the poor. Hazrat Umar (RA) managed it himself. Special care was taken of orphaned children. A stipend was fixed for children from the very day of their birth. He used to patrol himself at night so that he could learn the conditions of the poor. Whatever sum remained from government expenditure was distributed among the Muslims. For the first time in the history of the world he introduced a system of pension. He had several canals dug to improve irrigation and means of transport.",
