   "theory": "Exercise\n\n1. Fill in the blanks with suitable words.\n\ni. ________ first presented the concept of the welfare state.\n\nii. Hazrat Umar (RA) divided the empire into ________ administrative provinces.\n\niii. The total number of seats of the Senate is ________ .\n\niv. The foremost condition for good governance is the rule of ________ .\n\nv. The new local and district system has completed its first fixed term ________ in 2005.\n\n2. Choose the correct answer.\n\ni. According to the 1973 constitution, what kind of state is Pakistan? (parliamentary, unitary, presidential, federal)\n\nii. What is the total number of seats in the Senate? (70, 80, 90, 104)\n\niii. How many total seats does the province of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa have in the National Assembly? (40, 42, 55, 44)\n\niv. After how many years is the election of the members of the National Assembly held? (3 years, 4 years, 5 years, 6 years)\n\nv. Into how many provinces had Hazrat Umar Farooq (RA) divided his empire? (4, 6, 7, 8)\n\n3. Write short answers.\n\ni. What measures did Hazrat Umar Farooq (RA) take for public welfare?\n\nii. What method did Hazrat Umar Farooq (RA) adopt for the appointment of officials?\n\niii. What are the special powers of the President of Pakistan?",
