     "text": "… saints and poets, the axis of the poetry was mysticism (tasawwuf) and love. From the literary point of view the scope of the Punjabi language is quite vast. In it work has been done in almost every genre of literature. In Punjabi literature the emphasis is basically on the subjects of spirituality, mysticism and love. The poetry of the Sufis is a precious treasure of Punjabi folk literature, and even today it is read and heard with great reverence and respect. The Sufi saints chose the Punjabi language to convey their message to the people because it was the common language of the people of that period, whereas Persian and Arabic were the languages of the royal court and the elite. Besides mysticism, social and political subjects too are prominently seen in the poetry of the Sufis. That is why their verse was extremely popular among the people.",
