     "text": "In Punjabi poetry, narrative (dastan-goi) too holds a special place, and Punjabi romantic tales are the custodians of traditions thousands of years old. Among Punjabi folk tales, Waris Shah’s “Heer Ranjha”, Hashim Shah’s “Sassi Punnun”, Fazal Shah’s “Sohni Mahiwal” and Hafiz Barkhurdar’s “Mirza Sahiban” gained the most fame. In these tales, besides poetry of high rank, a full glimpse of the historical, religious and social life of the Punjab of that time is seen.",
