   "content": "<p>… are used and wasted.</p><p>II. Discontent, disaffection and restlessness arise in the lower class.</p><p>Therefore, appropriate measures and planning are needed to restrain the wealthy from this.</p><p>5. Reduction in unemployment</p><p>In Pakistan unemployment is increasing day by day. As many employment opportunities as possible should be created in the private sector. Attention should be given to acquiring technical education, and employment in the private sector should be encouraged. To control this, planning is extremely necessary.</p><p>6. Foreign loans and investment</p><p>Through economic planning we can find out how much foreign aid is needed for development programmes. Accordingly foreign investors can be encouraged to invest for the completion of various projects. Moreover loans can be taken from international financial institutions.</p><p>In Pakistan economic planning is necessary also so that those objectives can be achieved which developing countries keep in view, for example increase in national income, increase in per-capita income, increase in employment, self-sufficiency in food production, stability in prices, a high rate of capital formation, reform of the balance of payments, etc.</p><p>Agriculture and economy</p><p>Pakistan is an agricultural country. In our economy agriculture has, in terms of importance, the status of a backbone. Most of Pakistan’s population earns its livelihood from agriculture, and the remaining people earn their livelihood from other occupations, that is industry and trade, communications, construction and services etc. 67 per cent of the people living in villages subsist directly or indirectly on agriculture. In 2002–03, 24 per cent of the GDP (Gross Domestic Products) was obtained from agriculture. Agriculture also provides raw material for many industries of the country. In Pakistan industry too depends on agriculture, because by it the income of farmers will increase, their purchasing power will increase. In this way new factories will be established. At present 60 per cent of the production of industries consists of agriculture.</p><p>Agricultural development</p><p>Modern implements</p><p>To increase agricultural production it is necessary that farmers use modern mechanical implements. At present mechanised cultivation in our country is on a small scale. These machines include combine harvesters, threshers, tube wells and tractors etc.</p><p>Chemical fertiliser</p><p>Now farmers are inclined towards the maximum use of fertiliser. During 1952–53 one thousand tons of fertiliser was used, while in 2002–03 twenty-four lakh tons of fertiliser was used.</p><p>Use of good seed</p><p>To increase production the use of pure and high-quality seed is necessary. In 2002–03, 148 tons of improved seed were distributed among farmers. In Pakistan four government-sector organisations exist for the supply and distribution of seed.</p><p>Better protection of plants</p><p>Among us 25 per cent of agricultural crops is wasted because of plant diseases. Its solution is necessary. The government’s Department of Plant Protection arranges the spraying of medicines on crops from below or from the air.</p>",
