   "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>1. Four alternative answers are given for each question below. Mark the correct answer.</p><p>i. In 2003–2004 what percentage of GDP was obtained from agriculture? (15 per cent, 20 per cent, 24 per cent, 30 per cent)</p><p>ii. At present how much of the production of industries consists of agriculture? (40 per cent, 50 per cent, 60 per cent, 65 per cent)</p><p>iii. Among us what percentage of agricultural crops is wasted because of plant diseases? (10 per cent, 15 per cent, 20 per cent, 25 per cent)</p><p>iv. In which year did the government take many industries into national ownership? (in 1970, in 1971, in 1972, in 1974)</p><p>v. According to the opinion of economists, on how much of the area of a country should there be forests? (25 per cent, 40 per cent, 60 per cent, 80 per cent)</p><p>vi. Economic planning in Pakistan began — (in 1950, in 1955, in 1960, in 1965)</p><p>2. Fill in the blanks.</p><p>i. Pakistan is a developing ________ country.</p><p>ii. In Pakistan ________ per cent of cultivation is irrigated by artificial irrigation.</p><p>iii. In Pakistan comprehensive economic planning began for the first time in ________ .</p><p>iv. At the time of the establishment of Pakistan there were only ________ medical colleges in the country.</p><p>3. Write short answers.</p><p>i. Why is economic planning done?</p><p>ii. What are the five important basic objectives of the new National Education Policy (1998–2010)?</p><p>iii. Write a few benefits of forests.</p><p>iv. State the important exports of Pakistan.</p><p>4. Review the state of economic planning in Pakistan.</p><p>5. What measures is the government taking to solve the agricultural problems of Pakistan?</p><p>6. State the reasons for Pakistan’s industrial backwardness and propose measures to increase industrial production.</p><p>7. Write a detailed note on the important exports and imports of Pakistan.</p><p>8. Throw light on the importance of natural resources in the economic development of Pakistan.</p><p>9. State the important points of Pakistan’s National Education Policy (1998–2010).</p><p>10. What is meant by IT? What efforts are being made in Pakistan for its promotion?</p>",
