   "content": "<p>… ; America’s effort is somehow to end the Islamic government of Iran.</p><p>In these new conditions revolutionary changes appeared in Pakistan’s foreign policy too. When in September 2001, after the suicide attacks on America, pressure increased on the Taliban government in Afghanistan from America and its allied countries, Pakistan too left the Taliban government and joined America and its allied countries for the elimination of terrorism.</p><p>Pakistan’s foreign policy fell victim to considerable pressure on the Kashmir front too. In international politics the armed movements of freedom are being put into the category of terrorism. In these conditions the Kashmir issue became quite complex. Although Pakistani leaders, on various fronts and in clear words, tried their best to make clear the difference between terrorism and freedom movements, despite this the international community did not agree to change its thinking. In view of these changing conditions Pakistan too had to reconsider its Kashmir policy. Although Pakistan still holds its principled position on Kashmir (that is, that the decision about Kashmir should be according to the wishes of the people there), its method has now changed. Pakistan’s effort now is that all the armed jihadi organisations of Kashmir be included, through talks, in the solution of the Kashmir issue, and that the Kashmir issue be resolved through talks.</p><p>In the changing conditions, because of Pakistan’s wise policies, Pakistan obtained considerable stability. America has given Pakistan the status of a non-NATO friendly country. Not only were all the sanctions which had been imposed because of Pakistan’s atomic explosions lifted; billions of dollars of not only economic aid was given, but the provision of military weapons too was announced from America. Following America’s example, other developed countries too increased relations with Pakistan; not only economic help was provided, but investment was also made in Pakistan. Because of the positive foreign and economic policies of the government, Pakistan’s economic condition became very stable.</p><p>In the present period Pakistan is playing a very important and positive role in international politics. It is hoped that if continuity remains in Pakistan’s foreign and internal policies, then, God willing, Pakistan will soon be included in the ranks of the developed countries of the world.</p>",
