   "content": "<p>Exercise</p><p>1. Four alternative answers are given below for each question. Choose the correct answer.</p><p>i. A border dispute arose between Pakistan and China — (in 1950, in 1963, in 1965, in 1971)</p><p>ii. The organisation of Regional Cooperation for Development was established — (in 1960, in 1964, in 1980, in 1984)</p><p>iii. The name of the organisation of Regional Cooperation for Development was changed — (in 1962, in 1964, in 1975, in 1984)</p><p>iv. Pakistan carried out atomic explosions — (in 1990, in 1997, in 1998, in 1999)</p><p>v. The Indus Waters Treaty was settled between Pakistan and India — (in 1950, in 1960, in 1964, in 1971)</p><p>vi. After the establishment of Pakistan, the first country to recognise Pakistan was — (Afghanistan, Iran, China, Saudi Arabia)</p><p>2. Fill in the blanks with suitable words.</p><p>1. The name of the organisation of Regional Cooperation for Development was changed to the Economic Cooperation Organisation in ________ .</p><p>2. In 1971 India helped the ________ in East Pakistan.</p><p>3. In September 2001 ________ attacks took place on America.</p><p>4. ________ recognised Pakistan first of all.</p><p>5. America has given Pakistan the status of a ________ friendly country.</p><p>3. Write the correct and incorrect answers separately from the following.</p><p>1. The relations of Pakistan and Afghanistan have been pleasant from the beginning.</p>",
