   "theory": "2. Iran is the only country which opposed Pakistan’s membership in the United Nations.\n\n3. Pakistan has always raised its voice against racial discrimination.\n\n4. Pakistan carried out atomic explosions in 1998.\n\n5. Pakistan had not recognised the Taliban government.\n\n4. Match the events given in column “A” with the years given in column “B”.\n\n5. Give short answers.\n\n1. What is meant by foreign policy?\n\n2. Write five basic principles of foreign policy.\n\n3. What is meant by the administrative troika?\n\n4. Regional Cooperation for Development\n\n5. Duties of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs\n\n6. The role of political parties and pressure groups in foreign policy\n\n7. Write a short note on Pakistan’s atomic explosions.\n\n8. What is meant by national security?\n\n6. What is meant by foreign policy? Write a note on the sources of the formation of Pakistan’s foreign policy.\n\n7. Write a comprehensive note on the objectives of Pakistan’s foreign policy.\n\n8. Describe the evolution of the relations of Pakistan and America.\n\n9. Explain the relations of Pakistan with the following countries: (a) Afghanistan (b) Iran (c) Saudi Arabia\n\n10. Why has Pakistan’s foreign policy been under pressure on the Kashmir issue?",
